            <ArticleTitle>Aspirin resistance and a single gene.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>805-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study examined the association of single nucleotide polymorphisms in 4 candidate genes in a cohort of subjects with aspirin resistance. Aspirin resistance was significantly associated with genetic variation in the platelet surface adenosine 5-diphosphate receptor gene P2Y1.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
